  "conclusions": [
    "Instrumented straight runs exactly reproduce all compared basic telemetry arrays.",
    "No chassis contact resultant was sampled in any of the six runs; pair identities and continuous-time contact census are unavailable.",
    "The H5.5/sigma3.5 straight run repeatedly rolls back/reclimbs and never satisfies bounded-motion v2 within15s. High front-wheel spin often occurs while unloaded.",
    "The H6/sigma4.5 straight run confirms bounded motion at5.9s and stays within a.178m XY diameter in the last5s despite full throttle, zero brake, loaded-wheel slip and essentially zero hub progress. Its launch is not a settled from-rest condition.",
    "All current right/left detours also fail on the broad near-start hill footprint; neither scene is a valid four-route demonstration yet.",
    "Recommend moving the broad H6/sigma4.5 hill later, preferably centerx0, then probing straight/left/right unchanged physics. This repairs launch and lets route separation develop. A later stationary stall cannot be guaranteed from these runs."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only20Hz chassis contact resultants; zero cannot rule out brief or cancelling contacts.",
    "Chassis reference height and vertical hub-radius gaps are not exact underbody clearance.",
    "Power is the existing runner torque/speed product; gear, slip and force observations do not establish an engine-power limit or tire-friction saturation by themselves.",
    "Large tire-model slip on an unloaded wheel is not evidence of useful traction.",
    "Bounded motion and failure to climb are distinct; rollback is not relabeled stationary stall."
  ]
}
